 "A1_2_b_scoring": {
  "rule": "arm (b) is scored against the frozen chain closed through E97's idle law (heat_q138t's update, model-q138t.json, E78's S), run on the REALIZED launch pattern: every dispatch record in the pass's runs.jsonl is on at its item's E78 S, and the loop starts at R0's start from the measured rest die (the 34-sensor mean over R0's last 120 s). The checkpoints and the plateau are read as predict_e144.describe reads them, over one launch period on a duty-cycled hold and 5 s otherwise, as rises over the last 120 s of the rest before each hold, with the frozen bands (+-1.30 C PASS at every checkpoint from 60 s and the plateau, +-2.60 C plateau FAIL). The f5473428 plan numbers are reported beside (b_plan_f5473428); when the run matches the plan they agree (self-test 2: within 0.02 C). The same reading scores H_H' and the subset.",
  "why": "the plan's 3.2 s of compute per 7.0 s cannot be produced (A1.1), and the frozen numbers assume a 50.6 C rest; scored at the realized pattern, (b) tests the model and not the harness's rounding or the room"
 },
 "A1_3_definitions": {
  "rest_die": "aifoundry3: the 34-sensor mean of the raw codes over the last 120 s of the rest before the hold (the anchor of arm (a)). aifoundry2: the firmware's whole-degree minshire[0] reading, mean over the last 120 s of the REST before the hold (the anchor of arm (a); score_e144.py reads it so)",
  "G2_regime": "floor when at least 98% of the samples over the hold's last 300 s read 600 MHz, else trip (E111, floor: 1.000; E133, trip: 0.887)",
  "G2_tests": "in the floor regime G2 tests the chain (rest die + 0.663 x 32.42 W); in the trip regime it tests the governor's hold at the 65/66 boundary, not the chain",
  "G2_backcheck": {
